WEBVTT

00:00:01.617 --> 00:00:05.518
There are many islands in the sea near Scotland.

00:00:05.578 --> 00:00:09.809
This story is about one of these islands.

00:00:09.869 --> 00:00:13.780
The name of the island is Lana.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.741
Lana isn't big, but it's very beautiful.

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.572
It's very quiet too.

00:00:21.632 --> 00:00:29.199
There are no houses or roads or cars on Lana, but there's a castle.

00:00:29.259 --> 00:00:33.216
The castle is very old.

00:00:33.276 --> 00:00:37.698
A young Scotsman lives in the castle.

00:00:37.758 --> 00:00:42.759
The Scotsman's name is Duncan McTavish.

00:00:42.819 --> 00:00:48.550
Duncan lives in the castle with his dog, Jock.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:53.372
Duncan is very happy on his island.

00:00:53.432 --> 00:00:56.600
He likes going for walks with Jock. 

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:01.720
He likes swimming and fishing in his little boat.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:06.242
There are many big rooms in Duncan's castle.

00:01:06.302 --> 00:01:14.906
They have a lot of old things in them, pictures and heavy tables, chairs and beds.

00:01:14.966 --> 00:01:20.210
In winter, the castle is very cold and dark.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:27.063
Duncan puts on a lot of electric lights in all the rooms.

00:01:27.123 --> 00:01:33.606
One Monday morning in April, Duncan gets a letter.

00:01:33.666 --> 00:01:37.248
What's this? He asks.
 
00:01:37.308 --> 00:01:40.000
He opens the letter.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:43.672
It's from the electricity company.

00:01:43.732 --> 00:01:52.166
Duncan reads, Electricity from October to March: £5,000.

00:01:52.226 --> 00:01:55.210
Oh! Duncan says.
 
00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:59.064
I haven't got £5,000.

00:01:59.124 --> 00:02:00.864
What can I do?

00:02:00.884 --> 00:02:04.115
He's very unhappy.

00:02:04.175 --> 00:02:13.048
I can do only one thing, sell my island and my castle.

00:02:13.108 --> 00:02:17.419
Duncan telephones a man in London.

00:02:17.479 --> 00:02:21.705
The man's name is Mr Moneybags.

00:02:21.765 --> 00:02:27.264
Mr Moneybags sells houses and castles.

00:02:27.324 --> 00:02:34.751
I want to sell my island and my castle, Duncan says.

00:02:34.811 --> 00:02:39.585
Okay, Mr Moneybags says.

00:02:39.645 --> 00:02:44.379
Two days later, he telephones Duncan.

00:02:44.439 --> 00:02:50.434
Leaping Larry wants to buy your island, he says.

00:02:50.494 --> 00:02:54.896
Leaping who? Duncan asks.
 
00:02:54.956 --> 00:02:57.016
Leaping Larry.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:03:01.517
You know, the famous American rock star.

00:03:01.577 --> 00:03:06.128
He wants to buy your island for his girlfriend.

00:03:06.188 --> 00:03:11.889
A rock star? Duncan says. Oh.
 
00:03:11.948 --> 00:03:16.889
He wants to see the island tomorrow afternoon.

00:03:16.949 --> 00:03:21.000
Mr Moneybags says, is that okay?

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:29.696
Yes, Duncan says. Yes, of course.
 
00:03:29.756 --> 00:03:37.862
Leaping Larry and his girlfriend are coming to the island by helicopter.

00:03:37.921 --> 00:03:40.254
They're very late.

00:03:40.314 --> 00:03:44.527
Duncan and Jock wait a long time.

00:03:44.587 --> 00:03:48.604
Then the helicopter arrives.

00:03:48.664 --> 00:03:53.892
A tall man with long dark hair gets down from it.

00:03:53.951 --> 00:03:57.614
He's about 45 years old.

00:03:57.674 --> 00:04:00.046
There's a girl with him.

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:05.430
She's about 20 and has long yellow hair.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:08.603
There's a small animal with her.

00:04:08.663 --> 00:04:13.307
The animal has long white hair.

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:16.600
Hi, the man says.

00:04:16.659 --> 00:04:18.790
I'm Leaping Larry.

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:23.090
And this is my girlfriend, Roxanne.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:26.350
Hi, Roxanne says.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:30.152
This is my dog, Bobo.

00:04:30.212 --> 00:04:33.452
Larry looks at the castle.

00:04:33.512 --> 00:04:38.243
Look at that old castle, Roxanne, he says.

00:04:38.303 --> 00:04:41.264
Don't you love it, honey?

00:04:41.324 --> 00:04:44.434
Roxanne doesn't smile.

00:04:44.494 --> 00:04:47.738
It's only an old castle.

00:04:47.797 --> 00:04:52.894
Leaping Larry and Roxanne go into the castle.

00:04:52.954 --> 00:04:55.106
It's very dark.

00:04:55.166 --> 00:04:57.978
Leaping Larry can't see.

00:04:58.038 --> 00:05:00.460
He falls down.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.634
Where are the lights? He asks.
 
00:05:04.694 --> 00:05:08.157
I'm sorry, Duncan says.

00:05:08.217 --> 00:05:10.780
There isn't any light.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:15.970
The company stopped my electricity this morning.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:21.028
I want some hot food, Roxanne says.

00:05:21.088 --> 00:05:27.481
I'm sorry, Duncan says, but I can't make hot food.

00:05:27.541 --> 00:05:30.712
I haven't got any electricity.

00:05:30.772 --> 00:05:33.723
But there is some cold food.

00:05:33.783 --> 00:05:39.550
Cold food, Roxanne says. No, thank you.
 
00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:45.444
I'm going to bed, but first I want a hot bath.

00:05:45.504 --> 00:05:48.992
And Bobo wants a bath too.

00:05:49.052 --> 00:05:55.874
I'm very sorry, Duncan says, but there's no hot water.

00:05:55.934 --> 00:06:00.606
No lights, no food, no hot water.

00:06:00.666 --> 00:06:05.408
Roxanne says, I don't like this place.

00:06:05.468 --> 00:06:12.082
Now, honey, Leaping Larry says, don't call me honey.

00:06:12.142 --> 00:06:17.109
Roxanne says, Let's go Bobo.

00:06:17.168 --> 00:06:21.342
Roxanne and Bobo go to bed.

00:06:21.402 --> 00:06:26.094
Larry and Duncan eat cold food and talk.

00:06:26.154 --> 00:06:28.516
Jock watches them.

00:06:28.576 --> 00:06:32.158
Suddenly Roxanne screams.

00:06:32.218 --> 00:06:36.612
Duncan, Larry and Jock run to her room.

00:06:36.672 --> 00:06:40.324
Roxanne is in bed with Bobo.

00:06:40.384 --> 00:06:44.893
Honey, what's wrong? Larry asks.
 
00:06:44.952 --> 00:06:48.134
There was a noise in the room.

00:06:48.194 --> 00:06:50.005
Roxanne says.

00:06:50.065 --> 00:06:52.107
What was it?

00:06:52.166 --> 00:06:55.108
Duncan starts to smile.

00:06:55.167 --> 00:06:59.710
Why are you smiling? Roxanne says.
 
00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.081
She's very angry.

00:07:02.141 --> 00:07:06.183
Look at Jock. Duncan says.
 
00:07:06.243 --> 00:07:09.314
Jock is under the bed.

00:07:09.374 --> 00:07:12.593
He has a mouse in his mouth.

00:07:12.653 --> 00:07:16.411
A mouse! Roxanne says.
 
00:07:16.471 --> 00:07:20.132
She screams again.

00:07:20.192 --> 00:07:26.173
In the morning Duncan and Leaping Larry are waiting.

00:07:26.233 --> 00:07:29.664
Roxanne and Bobo are late.

00:07:29.724 --> 00:07:33.625
They get up at 11 o'clock.

00:07:33.685 --> 00:07:37.626
Good morning, Duncan says.

00:07:37.686 --> 00:07:40.867
Roxanne doesn't answer.

00:07:40.926 --> 00:07:46.850
She says to Larry, Larry, I don't like this place.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:49.192
I want to go home.

00:07:49.252 --> 00:07:52.383
But honey, Larry says.

00:07:52.443 --> 00:07:57.136
Don't call me honey, Roxanne says.

00:07:57.196 --> 00:08:02.709
This castle is old, dark and very cold.

00:08:02.769 --> 00:08:08.023
There's no electricity, no food, and no hot water.

00:08:08.082 --> 00:08:10.214
And I don't like it.

00:08:10.274 --> 00:08:12.808
Do you understand?

00:08:12.868 --> 00:08:16.172
Listen, honey, Larry says.

00:08:16.232 --> 00:08:19.716
We can build a big new house here.

00:08:19.775 --> 00:08:24.630
Our friends from California can come and stay.

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:27.492
Duncan looks at Jock.

00:08:27.552 --> 00:08:30.576
Jock looks at Duncan.

00:08:30.636 --> 00:08:38.268
Build a big new house, they think. Oh, no.
 
00:08:38.328 --> 00:08:45.036
Leaping Larry says, we want to see the island.

00:08:45.096 --> 00:08:51.548
Okay, Duncan says, we can go in my boat.

00:08:51.608 --> 00:08:57.069
Duncan, Larry and Roxanne get into Duncan's boat.

00:08:57.129 --> 00:08:59.590
Jock gets in too.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:02.810
Bobo is with Roxanne.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:09.376
It's a beautiful day, but Roxanne isn't happy.

00:09:09.436 --> 00:09:12.810
What do you do all day?"

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:15.221
She asks Duncan.

00:09:15.281 --> 00:09:19.272
I go for walks, Duncan says.

00:09:19.332 --> 00:09:25.533
Sometimes I swim, and sometimes I catch fish.

00:09:25.593 --> 00:09:28.853
Oh! Roxanne says.
 
00:09:28.913 --> 00:09:32.164
That isn't very interesting.

00:09:32.224 --> 00:09:35.504
Listen, honey, Larry says.

00:09:35.564 --> 00:09:38.656
We can make the island interesting.

00:09:38.716 --> 00:09:41.818
I know people with film companies.

00:09:41.878 --> 00:09:44.798
They can come here and make films.

00:09:44.858 --> 00:09:47.429
Hundreds of films.

00:09:47.489 --> 00:09:50.160
Duncan looks at Jock.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:53.250
Jock looks at Duncan.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:56.742
Film companies, they think.

00:09:56.802 --> 00:10:04.258
Oh, no. Duncan is very unhappy.
 
00:10:04.318 --> 00:10:09.616
He doesn't want to sell his island and his castle to Larry.

00:10:09.676 --> 00:10:15.662
He doesn't want film companies or Larry's friends on the island.

00:10:15.722 --> 00:10:18.584
But what can Duncan do?

00:10:18.644 --> 00:10:23.558
The electricity company wants £5,000.

00:10:23.618 --> 00:10:25.880
He has no money.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:29.548
He can't stay in his castle.

00:10:29.608 --> 00:10:35.538
Duncan, Larry and Roxanne are all sitting in Duncan's boat.

00:10:35.598 --> 00:10:38.710
Jock and Bobo are with them.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:43.374
Suddenly, Jock sees a rabbit on the island.

00:10:43.434 --> 00:10:46.476
Jock loves catching rabbits.

00:10:46.536 --> 00:10:51.810
He jumps into the sea and starts to swim to the island.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:56.304
Bobo thinks, this is interesting.

00:10:56.364 --> 00:10:59.108
And he jumps in too.

00:10:59.168 --> 00:11:03.832
Bobo is in the water, Roxanne screams.

00:11:03.892 --> 00:11:08.055
Jump into the sea, Larry. Get Bobo.
 
00:11:08.115 --> 00:11:10.996
But Larry doesn't move.

00:11:11.056 --> 00:11:15.490
Why are you waiting? Roxanne says.
 
00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:17.460
Jump in.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:20.613
But honey, Larry says.

00:11:20.673 --> 00:11:22.714
I can't swim.

00:11:22.774 --> 00:11:26.446
Can't swim? Roxanne says.
 
00:11:26.506 --> 00:11:29.512
She is very angry.

00:11:29.572 --> 00:11:35.021
Look, Duncan says, Bobo is okay.

00:11:35.081 --> 00:11:37.813
He's having a good time.

00:11:37.873 --> 00:11:46.460
Bobo is swimming in the water with Jock, but Roxanne is very angry with Larry.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:52.966
You don't love me. She says, and you don't love me.
 
00:11:53.026 --> 00:11:57.400
Larry says, you only love Bobo.

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:01.078
You're right. Roxanne says.
 
00:12:01.137 --> 00:12:05.780
She stands in the boat and starts to hit Larry.

00:12:05.840 --> 00:12:09.382
Don't do that, Duncan says.

00:12:09.442 --> 00:12:11.452
The boat moves.

00:12:11.512 --> 00:12:15.264
Roxanne falls into the water.

00:12:15.324 --> 00:12:18.056
She starts to scream.

00:12:18.116 --> 00:12:22.128
Roxanne is making a lot of noise.

00:12:22.188 --> 00:12:26.630
Jock sees Roxanne in the water with Bobo.

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:28.646
What are they doing?

00:12:28.706 --> 00:12:31.404
Are they playing a new game?

00:12:31.464 --> 00:12:34.274
Jock wants to play too.

00:12:34.334 --> 00:12:37.026
He swims to Bobo.

00:12:37.086 --> 00:12:41.518
Go away! Roxanne screams.
 
00:12:41.578 --> 00:12:45.670
Duncan brings the boat near Roxanne.

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:48.862
Roxanne gets into the boat.

00:12:48.922 --> 00:12:52.814
Then Bobo gets into the boat.

00:12:52.874 --> 00:12:57.246
Roxanne is very angry.

00:12:57.306 --> 00:13:01.108
Take me back to California.

00:13:01.168 --> 00:13:06.908
Now, she says to Larry.

00:13:06.969 --> 00:13:15.940
Later, Larry, Roxanne and Bobo get into their helicopter.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:19.681
Goodbye, Duncan says.

00:13:19.741 --> 00:13:23.652
Larry and Roxanne don't answer.

00:13:23.712 --> 00:13:27.070
The helicopter goes away.

00:13:27.130 --> 00:13:29.988
Duncan smiles at Jock.

00:13:30.048 --> 00:13:32.658
He's very happy.

00:13:32.719 --> 00:13:39.160
Leaping Larry isn't going to buy our island, he says.

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:41.610
That's good.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:46.582
But Duncan has big money problems.

00:13:46.642 --> 00:13:51.123
Leaping Larry doesn't want to buy the island.

00:13:51.184 --> 00:13:57.968
But where can Duncan get £5,000 for the electricity company?

00:13:58.028 --> 00:14:04.262
Later, Duncan telephones Mr Moneybags in London.

00:14:04.322 --> 00:14:10.384
Leaping Larry telephoned me, Mr Moneybags says.

00:14:10.444 --> 00:14:13.355
He doesn't like your island.

00:14:13.415 --> 00:14:16.146
He doesn't want to buy it.

00:14:16.206 --> 00:14:20.237
And I'm not going to sell it for you now.

00:14:20.297 --> 00:14:25.530
It's your problem. Goodbye.
 
00:14:25.590 --> 00:14:30.836
Duncan goes for a long walk with Jock.

00:14:30.896 --> 00:14:33.496
He's very unhappy.

00:14:33.556 --> 00:14:41.282
They walk to a place across the island, and there Duncan sees a girl.

00:14:41.342 --> 00:14:46.344
She's looking at the sea, and she's painting a picture.

00:14:46.404 --> 00:14:50.397
Near her is a small boat.

00:14:50.456 --> 00:14:55.219
Good afternoon, Duncan says.

00:14:55.278 --> 00:14:58.370
The girl looks at Duncan.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.381
She's beautiful.

00:15:00.441 --> 00:15:02.722
He likes her.

00:15:02.782 --> 00:15:06.166
Who are you? She asks.
 
00:15:06.226 --> 00:15:09.598
What do you want?

00:15:09.658 --> 00:15:14.191
I'm Duncan McTavish, Duncan says.

00:15:14.251 --> 00:15:15.912
I live here.

00:15:15.972 --> 00:15:18.624
Lana is my island.

00:15:18.684 --> 00:15:22.478
And this is my dog, Jock.

00:15:22.538 --> 00:15:25.062
Jock looks at the girl.

00:15:25.122 --> 00:15:27.676
He likes her too.

00:15:27.736 --> 00:15:32.110
Lana is your island, the girl says.

00:15:32.170 --> 00:15:35.832
Oh, I'm Jean Stewart.

00:15:35.892 --> 00:15:37.554
I'm a teacher.

00:15:37.614 --> 00:15:41.228
I work in a school across the sea.

00:15:41.288 --> 00:15:45.962
Today is a holiday and the school is closed.

00:15:46.022 --> 00:15:49.134
I came here in my boat.

00:15:49.194 --> 00:15:52.370
I wanted to paint your island.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:58.367
The light is very good, and the colours are very beautiful.

00:15:58.427 --> 00:16:01.948
I can paint good pictures here.

00:16:02.008 --> 00:16:05.480
Duncan looks at Jean's picture.

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:08.001
Yes, he says.

00:16:08.061 --> 00:16:11.072
Your picture is very good.

00:16:11.132 --> 00:16:14.343
Thank you, Jean says.

00:16:14.403 --> 00:16:18.975
Duncan and Jean talk for a long time.

00:16:19.035 --> 00:16:22.660
Where do you live, Jean asks?

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:26.716
I live in a castle, Duncan says.

00:16:26.776 --> 00:16:29.116
Come and see it.

00:16:29.176 --> 00:16:33.690
Duncan, Jean and Jock go to the castle.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:38.682
Your castle is beautiful, Jean says.

00:16:38.743 --> 00:16:44.656
Yes, Duncan says, but it's very cold and dark.

00:16:44.716 --> 00:16:47.240
There's no electricity.

00:16:47.300 --> 00:16:49.764
I have no money.

00:16:49.824 --> 00:16:56.546
I love my island very much, but I can't make money from it.

00:16:56.606 --> 00:16:59.566
Jean looks at the castle.

00:16:59.626 --> 00:17:04.938
Suddenly she says, yes, you can.

00:17:04.998 --> 00:17:08.137
How? Duncan asks.
 
00:17:08.197 --> 00:17:13.338
People can come here for holidays, Jean says.

00:17:13.398 --> 00:17:17.211
They can paint pictures of your island.

00:17:17.271 --> 00:17:19.362
I can teach them.

00:17:19.422 --> 00:17:22.924
And they can stay in your castle.

00:17:22.984 --> 00:17:26.397
We can make a lot of money.

00:17:26.456 --> 00:17:29.608
Duncan looks at Jock.

00:17:29.668 --> 00:17:32.920
Jock looks at Duncan.

00:17:32.981 --> 00:17:37.603
You're right, Duncan says.

00:17:37.663 --> 00:17:44.668
Now, McTavish Painting Holidays are very famous.

00:17:44.728 --> 00:17:49.292
Every year, many visitors come to the island.

00:17:49.352 --> 00:17:51.804
They stay in the castle.

00:17:51.864 --> 00:17:56.198
They go for walks and paint beautiful pictures.

00:17:56.258 --> 00:18:00.231
They take their pictures back to their homes.

00:18:00.291 --> 00:18:05.719
The rooms in the castle aren't cold and dark now.

00:18:05.779 --> 00:18:09.775
Duncan and Jean have a lot of money.

00:18:09.835 --> 00:18:14.218
There is no problem with the electricity company.

00:18:14.278 --> 00:18:18.430
And Jean makes very good food.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:22.732
The visitors are very happy.

00:18:22.792 --> 00:18:27.256
Duncan and Jean are married now.

00:18:27.316 --> 00:18:32.348
They have two children, a boy and a girl.

00:18:32.408 --> 00:18:36.670
Jock loves playing with the children.

00:18:36.731 --> 00:18:41.404
Duncan often sits in his little boat.

00:18:41.464 --> 00:18:48.480
Sometimes he catches a fish, but usually he sleeps.

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:55.000
He's a happy man.